.SH "LOG"
.SH "NAME"
.PP
\fIlog\fP \- log queries

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
By just using \fIlog\fP you dump all queries on standard output. Options exist to tweak the output. Note that for
busy servers logging will incur a performance hit. The \fIlog\fP handler only logs properties of the incoming query.

.PP
Enabling or disabling the \fIlog\fP handler only affects the query logging, any other logging from
testserv will show up regardless.

.SH "SYNTAX"
.PP
.RS

.nf
log

.fi
.RE

.PP
A typical example looks like this:

.PP
.RS

.nf
::1:50759 \- 29008 "A IN example.org. udp 41 4096" NOERROR qr,rd,ra,ad,do 68 QUERY

.fi
.RE
